    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Carson had looked like she wanted to crawl out of her own skin when Rosie wrote MARIGOLD? on the whiteboard",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4611
        },
        {
          "text": "The way she braced herself whenever somebody offered help",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4870
        },
        {
          "text": "The way she looked at the ranch when I’d driven her home, as if every broken fence post was somehow a personal failure",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4988
        },
        {
          "text": "There had been love there. And guilt. A hell of a lot of guilt",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5194
        }
      ],
      "words": 69
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "You came home from that hospital different",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5551
        },
        {
          "text": "You lost something before him that I never knew how to help you grieve",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5595
        },
        {
