    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "YOUTH BARREL FINALS — CARSON ROME & BLUEBERRY — WILLOW CREEK, GA",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7006
        },
        {
          "text": "Carson didn’t. That was the first thing I noticed. She was completely still, focused on the task at hand",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7647
        },
        {
          "text": "Blueberry dropped into the turn. Carson moved with her like they weren’t two separate entities, but rather one unit",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8251
        },
        {
          "text": "For a second, they looked less like a rider and horse and more like one damn animal",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8367
        }
      ],
      "words": 70
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "He had been younger too. Less gray in his hair. Broader through the shoulders. A cigar pinched between two fingers even ",
          "ok": true,
