      "words": 58
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "James walked over, wrapped one hand around the post, and shook it. It moved and he made me redo the entire thing. I’d be",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17480
        },
        {
          "text": "That had been James Rome. The type of man who built things expecting them to outlive him",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 18139
        },
        {
          "text": "The only person who seemed to believe every failing board and overdue bill was proof she’d disappointed him was Carson h",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 18372
        }
      ],
      "words": 88
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“She said she doesn’t need Carson to agree for us to determine whether two hay wagons are safe.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 20003
        },
        {
          "text": "“James taught you enough.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 20448
        },
        {
          "text": "Dad walked toward the bays. I looked at the parts sheet again. Going to Marigold Ranch shouldn’t have interested me. And",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 20961
        },
        {
          "text": "It did. All because I was eager to see one person",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 21086
        }
      ],
      "words": 57
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Then I heard Carson. “No, Earl, we aren’t moving her.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22498
        },
        {
          "text": "“Don’t do that.” There was no anger in her voice. That somehow made it firmer. “If something changes with one of the cal",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 23559
        },
        {
          "text": "Something passed over her face. Utter exhaustion. She rubbed both hands against her jeans. “One thing at a time.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 24113
        }
      ],
      "words": 80
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Slowly, she turned her head toward me. “How do you know that?”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 26708
        },
        {
          "text": "I probably could’ve lied. Dad could’ve told me. Half the town probably knew. Instead, I shoved my hands into my pockets ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 26769
        },
        {
          "text": "I rested my forearms against the fence. “My dad undersold you.” She glanced at me. “James undersold you.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 27277
        }
      ],
      "words": 65
    },
    {
      "block": "原句14",
      "no": 14,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“I thought I had time.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 29574
        },
        {
          "text": "Four words. They landed harder than everything I’d watched the night before. I thought about my spare bedroom. The boxes",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 29596
        },
        {
          "text": "“Yeah,” I said quietly. “I think everybody does.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 29852
        }
      ],
      "words": 59
    },
    {
      "block": "原句15",
      "no": 15,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The door groaned open. She didn’t look at me. I didn’t offer to help with the other one. Not because she couldn’t use it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 30786
        },
        {
          "text": "They weren’t just asking Carson to host a festival. They were asking her to open a door she’d kept shut for five years",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 32354
        },
        {
          "text": "They remembered what Marigold Ranch had been. A place that made magic feel real",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 32587
        }
      ],
      "words": 86
    }
